  "interpretation": [
    "Some local/global instructions are necessary for argument/result passing and checked owner/borrow/default-zero semantics. The new model does not require redundant copies or eager copying of every unchanged aggregate lane.",
    "Exact historical replay proves the 2,076,028-byte predecessor. Before this cleanup, growth to 16,220,693B included 10,319,186B of added local/global instructions (72.95% of total growth); embedded data shrank. These are static category differences, not a controlled compiler-only regression attribution.",
    "The prior heap-pointer representation made record transport one word while moving allocation and field accesses into runtime storage. The current recursive physical representation can expand control/call boundaries into many word transfers. Preserve ownership requirements while delaying materialization and sharing unchanged lanes.",
    "This bounded cleanup removes 685,121B (4.22%) but leaves 15,535,572B. A measured representation/transport pilot is still needed for the much larger remaining gap; no promise of 1-2MB follows from this slice."
  ],
  "next": "Prototype immutable word/immediate references and selective materialization of genuinely differing aggregate merge/result lanes within existing Value/Core semantics. Measure large result/control transport before another ABI rewrite. Keep type/owner/read/variant checks, explicit copies, loop/backedge correctness and repeated invocation zeros.",
